  "about": "The playful word on a turn's working row: present while the Cell works, past once it is done. Each verb is [present, past, span, topics, ...flags]: the past form is written out, never derived; span is how the past meets its clock (\"Noodled for 3m\", \"Sent it in 3m\"); topics are the prompts it suits. A favourite comes up twice as often; a topic-only verb waits for its topic and stays out of the general pool. A prompt's earliest keyword in its first 400 characters picks its topic. Playful, kind, work-shaped, one word or two short ones; never one a person could take for real work.",
